SUMMARY:Convergent Bodies: First Leap
DESCRIPTION:Image Credit: Bianca Tainsh (microscopy image with Sandra Tuszy
 nska) Convergent Bodies is a visceral self-identification with other inter
 species bodies and the emergence of a speculative posthuman future where t
 echnology is applied as ecological steward and interlocutor for entangleme
 nt with the more-than-human. In an 11-week OCCUPY residency\, artist Bianc
 a Tainsh has been visualising this concept through experimental juxtaposit
 ions of a vast exploratory archive of organic artefacts and digital docume
 ntation\, and an accumulating body of aesthetic and conceptual research ex
 ploring microscopic and subterranean realms and the relational and metaphy
 sical entanglement of all species. Unlike Haeckel's Art Forms in Nature \,
  Tainsh's archive seeks the wild asymmetries of decay\, sexual manifestati
 on\, and symbiosis. Convergent Bodies: First Leap is the initial manifesta
 tion of a new body of work that will take its cues from Tainsh's residency
  experiments. #block-f1e6d2ae56c80dd9e160 { } #block-f1e6d2ae56c80dd9e160 
